####################################################################
# B. FULL-APP xcodebuild build test — DEFERRED (macOS-pending)     #
####################################################################

The prompt gate's two xcodebuild steps —
  xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 16' build test
  xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync-macOS build test
require linking the KMP Shared.xcframework into the whole-app target. They
DO NOT GO GREEN on this host, blocked exclusively by PRE-EXISTING, UNRELATED
issues (identical to the precedent recorded for P-0010-ToolCard,
0180-AlertMessageEditor, 0231-FSMTimelineChart in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md).
This surface contributes ZERO of those errors.

Evidence the blockers are pre-existing and not this surface:

  B1. Shared.xcframework cannot be staged on this host.
      `cd apps/shared && ./gradlew :core:assembleSharedXCFramework` runs the
      Kotlin/Native toolchain (offline cache + JDK17 present, Xcode selected via
      DEVELOPER_DIR) but the release XCFramework assembly (all device/simulator/
      macOS slices) does not finish within the host build window; on CI it is
      produced on a macos-latest runner (ADR-012 matrix; tracked as a
      macOS-pending item since S3-0001-kmp-scaffold). Without the staged
      framework every app-target file that `import Shared` fails to compile —
      none of which is this surface (see B3).

  B2. Pre-existing parallel-merge symbol collisions in the app target:
        - `public struct DashboardWidgetSize` is defined in 15 files under
          apps/apple/{Sources,TeslaSync}/** (redefinition error). This surface
          defines it 0 times.
        - 256 co-located *.Tests.swift / *.ModelTests.swift under dashboard-widgets/
          + feature-views/ `import XCTest` into the app target (the established
          repo pattern; reconciled by the P99 acceptance gate's test-target
          wiring on macos-latest). This surface follows the same co-location
          convention (1 file) — it introduces no new class of breakage.
        - macOS development code-signing identities are absent on this host.

  B3. This surface is fully decoupled from all of the above:
        - `import Shared` occurrences in shared-surfaces/: 0
        - `struct DashboardWidgetSize` in shared-surfaces/: 0
        - It depends only on Foundation / SwiftUI / Observation / OSLog and the
          Shared-free design tokens (Tokens.swift + TSMaterial.swift) — which is
          exactly why Part A (isolated SwiftPM build + 27 tests + both-SDK
          typecheck) is green.

Resolution: deferred to p4-apple/P99-0001-apple-acceptance-gate (runs on
macos-latest with the KMP framework built + signing identities). A row is
appended to apps/macos-pending-verifications.md per that doc's protocol.

Verification command on macOS CI (unchanged from the prompt gate):
  cd apps/apple && DEVELOPER_DIR=/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer \
    xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync \
    -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 16' build test

